Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, potential uses and likely filter conditions
• year / month / day – date pieces; filter for 2005‑2015, build a proper DATE  
• latitude / longitude – keep to return the exact position of the observation  
• wind_speed – numeric value (in tenths of m s‑1); must be non‑NULL and not NaN; will be averaged  
Typical WHERE pieces  
    year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015  
    wind_speed IS NOT NULL  
    NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)  

Below are ten exploratory → analytical BigQuery statements (all read‑only SELECTs) that gradually lead to the final answer.  
All tables come from the same dataset and share the prefix ​icoads_core_.  

```sql
-- 1) Description: quick glance at 2005 table, non‑missing wind‑speed rows
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: look at a later year (2008) and convert the stored
--  tenths‑of‑m s‑1 units to true m s‑1 for human reading
SELECT year, month, day,
       latitude, longitude,
       wind_speed/10.0 AS wind_speed_mps
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2008`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: distinct years present across *all* icoads_core_* tables
SELECT DISTINCT year
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: daily average wind speed (m s‑1) for a single table (2010)
SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
       AVG(wind_speed)/10.0 AS avg_wind_mps
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2010`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date
ORDER BY avg_wind_mps DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: sample of unified data (2005‑2007) via UNION ALL
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2005`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
UNION ALL
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2006`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
UNION ALL
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_2007`
WHERE wind_speed IS NOT NULL AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: use a wildcard table reference for all years,
--  keep only the 2005‑2015 window and preview 20 rows
SELECT year, month, day, latitude, longitude, wind_speed
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
  AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: compute the maximum single‑report wind speed (m s‑1)
--  per year in the study period
SELECT year,
       MAX(wind_speed)/10.0 AS max_report_wind_mps
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
  AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY year
ORDER BY max_report_wind_mps DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: find the five strongest *single* observations
--  (no daily averaging) in 2005‑2015
SELECT year, month, day,
       latitude, longitude,
       wind_speed/10.0 AS wind_speed_mps
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
  AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
ORDER BY wind_speed_mps DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: daily average computed over all reports regardless
--  of location (just to see how a pure‑date grouping behaves)
SELECT DATE(year,month,day) AS obs_date,
       AVG(wind_speed)/10.0 AS avg_wind_mps
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
  AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date
ORDER BY avg_wind_mps DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: FINAL ANSWER – top‑5 latitude/longitude/day
--  combinations that exhibit the highest *daily‑average* wind speeds
--  between 2005 and 2015 (inclusive).  Wind speed converted to m s‑1.
SELECT
  DATE(year,month,day)             AS obs_date,
  latitude,
  longitude,
  AVG(wind_speed)/10.0             AS avg_wind_mps
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_icoads.icoads_core_*`
WHERE year BETWEEN 2005 AND 2015
  AND wind_speed IS NOT NULL
  AND NOT IS_NAN(wind_speed)
GROUP BY obs_date, latitude, longitude
ORDER BY avg_wind_mps DESC
LIMIT 5;
```
